# membrane-health.rq — a membrane's own health, read off the act that closed it.
#
# `_seal` mints an `etkl:MembraneValidation` recording that a validation HAPPENED and what
# the engine returned (spec 2026-08-25 §4.2). This states what that verdict, together with
# the propositions still held at the boundary, MEANS about the document holon:
#   Compromised — a validation act that says the interior did not conform;
#   Weakened    — it conformed, and a candidate concept is still held at the membrane;
#   Intact      — it conformed, and nothing is held.
# `Intact` says NOTHING about how much of the document was read (spec §4.4): a document with
# escalated bands and zero candidates is correctly Intact. `score` is the other signal.
#
# GATE (CLAUDE.md §8): AXIOM, derivation form. Open world, evidence-positive, idempotent. It
# decides nothing — the conformance judgement was already made by the membrane and recorded
# at the call site; this states its consequence.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVIDENCE-POSITIVE, in all three arms (spec §4.3 invariant 1). Each value is derived from a
# triple that is PRESENT: `Compromised` from an act whose `sh:conforms` is `false`,
# `Weakened` from a candidate that exists, `Intact` from an act whose `sh:conforms` is
# `true`. `Intact` is NEVER derived from a violation not being in the graph — inferring from
# the absence of a violation is precisely what the gate forbids in its own words, and it is
# why the health is read off an ACT rather than off the graph's quietness.
#   The same rule is what makes the third row of spec §4.5 a consequence rather than a
#   special case: with `validate_shapes=False` no act is minted, this WHERE has no support,
#   and the document carries NO health triple. Absence, never a fourth state.
#   Pinned by tests/etkl/test_membrane_health.py —
#   `test_the_three_values_discriminate` (the falsifying oracle: collapse the IF to a
#   constant and it fails) and `test_a_document_compiled_without_the_membrane_has_no_health`.
#
# THE QUERY REFUSES TO GUESS (spec §4.3 invariant 5; review B6). `?conforms = false`, never
# `!?conforms`: the `!` operator would run SPARQL's effective-boolean-value coercion, under
# which an untyped `"false"` is TRUE and a REFUSING membrane would report itself Intact — a
# failure upward, and silent. The `datatype(?conforms) = xsd:boolean` filter closes the same
# hole from the other side: a slipped datatype yields no health triple AT ALL rather than a
# wrong one, failing downward into the silence the paragraph above already licenses.
#   Pinned by `test_a_slipped_datatype_yields_no_health_rather_than_intact`, which asserts
#   the OUTPUT IS EMPTY for both an untyped and an xsd:string verdict.
#
# HOLON-SCOPED CLOSED WORLD (spec §4.3 invariant 2). `?held` uses two negation-flavoured
# constructs and both are scoped to this one document's holon, which CLAUDE.md §8 names as
# the closure boundary:
#   * the `FILTER NOT EXISTS` is scoped to a BOUND `?cand` — it selects between two PRESENT
#     readings of that candidate (proposed, or reviewed by a promotion decision) and never
#     derives a fact from an absence in the wider world. Same construct, same classification
#     and same licence as `escalation-furnish.rq`'s supersession guard.
#   * the enclosing `EXISTS` closes over the graph it is run on — which is why the site
#     constraint below is not optional.
#   The `?pd a iladub:PromotionDecision` type clause STAYS although it is currently
#   redundant: it is the guard against the IRI collision of spec §2.2.
#   Pinned by `test_a_reviewed_candidate_no_longer_weakens_the_membrane`, and it is the ONLY
#   test that can pin it: MEASURED, deleting this `FILTER NOT EXISTS` changes the derived
#   value on exactly one of four graph states — a candidate that a promotion decision REVIEWS
#   (Intact as shipped, Weakened without it). Every other state, the whole shipped fixture
#   corpus included, is blind to it.
#
#   SITE CONSTRAINT this places on the caller: run this over ONE DOCUMENT'S GRAPH, never a
#   union of several. The binding reason is not the closed-world scoping above (true, and
#   insufficient) but SUBJECT-IRI COLLISION: `_DOC` is one constant IRI shared by every
#   document (`compile.py:22`), so `?doc` binds to the same subject in every graph and a
#   union puts two health values on one subject, with nothing at runtime to refuse them —
#   MEASURED in spec §4.3 invariant 3 (three triples on one `?doc`, `Compromised` AND
#   `Intact`), not asserted here. `_seal` satisfies the constraint by construction: it runs
#   over the single graph it was handed.
#   THE SAME COLLISION IS REACHABLE WITHOUT A UNION, and that one was measured in this loop:
#   re-entering `_seal` with a DIFFERENT verdict derives a second value onto the same `?doc`.
#   The site answers it — `document.py` removes the stale value before re-deriving, pinned by
#   `test_re_entering_the_seam_leaves_exactly_one_health_value` — because a CONSTRUCT cannot
#   retract, and health is minted after the membrane has run so no shape sees it.
#
# IDEMPOTENT, AND IT NEVER READS ITS OWN PRODUCT (spec §4.3 invariant 4). No pattern in the
# WHERE mentions `etkl:membraneHealth` or `etkl:CompiledDocumentHolon`, so re-running over a
# graph that already carries the health triple re-derives exactly it, and the derivation
# stays a pure function of the evidence. Idempotence is structural rather than asserted.
#   Pinned by `test_health_is_re_derived_not_stored`: strip both constructed triples, re-run,
#   and the re-derived set equals what was stripped.
PREFIX etkl:   <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#>
PREFIX iladub: <https://w3id.org/iladub#>
PREFIX prov:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>
PREFIX rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX sh:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>
PREFIX xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
CONSTRUCT {
  ?doc rdf:type            etkl:CompiledDocumentHolon ;
       etkl:membraneHealth ?health .
}
WHERE {
  # THE ACT, never the graph's quietness. `prov:used` names the holon that was validated, so
  # `?doc` is bound from the evidence and never written here.
  ?act rdf:type      etkl:MembraneValidation ;
       sh:conforms   ?conforms ;
       prov:used     ?doc .
  # refuses to guess — see above
  FILTER(datatype(?conforms) = xsd:boolean)
  # a proposition still HELD at this membrane: proposed, and no promotion decision reviews it
  BIND(EXISTS { ?cand rdf:type iladub:CandidateConcept .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?pd rdf:type  iladub:PromotionDecision ;
                                        iladub:reviews ?cand } }
       AS ?held)
  # `?conforms = false`, never `!?conforms` — see THE QUERY REFUSES TO GUESS above
  BIND(IF(?conforms = false,
          etkl:Compromised,
          IF(?held, etkl:Weakened, etkl:Intact)) AS ?health)
}
